Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:10:06 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 14/49] Plutonium: tags and groups on windows and tabs, the
 Super+Tab overlay

Every window and tab carries a list of tags; the first (the thread that
started a window's client, or a tab's creation tag) is fixed, shells add
and remove the rest. Shells describe their tags as groups (label, owning
shell), kept in local state. The broker gains tag, group and shell
methods and focus-request events.

Super+Tab opens a native overlay in Ash listing shells, windows and tabs
by group: switch, show an item in its owner shell, turn shells on and
off, reload, edit, add and remove them, and tag items.

